nodecode-doctorpack is a rewrite of godhiraj-code's godhiraj-code/hermes-doctorpack:
https://github.com/godhiraj-code/hermes-doctorpack
commit ac00ace14ea9210e2e02a7b978cf4bc51eec2d8f
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Dhiraj Das (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the three tools (config audit, plugin check, postmortem) and the
slash command, in Common Lisp against the Nodecode cell contract. The finding model
(ok/warn/fail/unknown, severity, confidence, evidence, recommendation), the overall
status ranking, the conservative rule that missing evidence is `unknown' and never
`fail', the redaction pass (assigned keys and tokens, bearer credentials, issuer-
prefixed token shapes, URL userinfo, email addresses and phone shapes), the log scan
with its lookback window and its error/warning word lists, the exclusive-creation
report naming, and the postmortem's markdown layout are the original's, carried over
line for line in intent and reimplemented here.

What was left out and why: the subject is the Nodecode home rather than the Hermes
home, so the checks read what this harness writes -- config.jsonc instead of
config.yaml, the cells/ folder instead of the plugins/ list, and the home's own
*.log files instead of Hermes's agent/gateway/errors logs. Hermes's approval mode
and its security.redact_secrets switch have no Nodecode counterpart, so the inline-
credential check stands in their place, and a cell folder that carries no .asd
stands in for Hermes's 'enabled and disabled at once' plugin conflict. The pip
distribution, the hermes plugin.yaml entry points and the CLI subcommand
registration are replaced by the cell's own declaration, and PyYAML by the cell's
line readers; nothing of the original's Python is bundled.
